.TH geectl-remote-devel-project 1  "geectl-remote-devel-project 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-devel\-project \- Show the devel project and devel package of a package, when it has one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote devel\-project\fR [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACKAGE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the devel project and devel package of a package, when it has one
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The target project the package lives in (default: openSUSE:Factory)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to look up
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
